PROJECT MANAGEMENT
AI-Powered Automated Inventory and Freshness Monitoring System for Small-Scale Retailers
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
1.   Executive Summary
This proposal defines the management plan for delivering the AI-powered inventory and freshness monitoring system within the period 01 July to 03 October 2026. The project will be divided into nine sprints. Early sprints focus on proposal, feasibility, requirements and architecture. Middle sprints focus on prototype and core implementation. Final sprints focus on integration, testing, demo preparation and final submission. The system will support small-scale retailers by allowing produce images to be captured through a mobile device, processed by an AI model and displayed in a dashboard with inventory and freshness status.
2.   Project Scope
In scope: mobile image capture, web administration dashboard, backend REST APIs, secure login, database, cloud/image storage, inventory alerts, freshness scores, analytics reports and AI classification service.
Out of scope: physical IoT sensors, smart scales, automatic procurement, supply-chain integration, financial accounting and tax filing modules.
 
